      "created_at": "2021-04-30T19:43:25Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-04-30T19:43:56Z",
      "body": "Hello @greyson-signal , most of these people are not tech-savvy at all, and they come to me for tech questions.\r\nIt was already a nightmare to move them from Messenger to WhatsApp, and I'm in no position (mentally speaking) to endure having to push yet another app into the family... So I really doubt they would willingly install it.\r\nWhile I can't of course be 100% certain that **all** of them (we're talking like 20-30 people) never installed Signal by mistake, I'm confident enough to assume there's an issue somewhere.\r\n\r\nIs it possible that someone is mass registering users for known/captured phones from marketing lists and whatnot?\r\nI don't recall, but I guess Signal requires an SMS verification? If that's the case then mass registration wouldn't _really_ be possible (unless there was a loophole somewhere, or a vulnerability somewhere).",
      "author_association": "NONE",
